# Files this package PUBLISHES into a consumer's own repository must be LF on
# disk in every checkout, including Windows ones.
#
# `vendor:publish` copies the bytes as they sit in vendor/. With the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows box — which is what the platform's dev
# machines run — a source install hands the consumer CRLF files, and the
# consumer's own `pint` run then reports `line_ending` and rewrites vendor-
# published files on its first CI run. Then again after every republish. The
# diff is noise, it is never reviewed, and it makes `vendor:publish --force`
# look like it changed something when it did not.
#
# Scoped to the published artefacts on purpose: marking the whole tree would
# renormalise every file in the repository in one unrelated commit.
*.stub text eol=lf
/config/*.php text eol=lf
